      "last_decision": {
        "at": "2026-10-20T16:15:38.475162+00:00",
        "symbol": "GOOG",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Stay flat on GOOG.NAS. Nothing new since the approved hold at 13:40 UTC resolves the dispute: still no Q3-26 10-Q, no 8-K-confirmed earnings date, and no verified scope or issuer statement on the Oct-20 Cloud outage. Fresh news adds only secondary items - a BofA note flagging Cloud/TPU Q3 upside (unverified, promotional-grade) and broader tech-led selling on AI-investment fears with oil rising - neither primary-verified nor thesis-changing. Price slipped from the prior packet's ~338.44-338.54 to 337.60/337.68, a routine dip within the 333-351 range and not the decisive 200-day break on volume that the invalidation trigger requires (the 200-day at 338.92 is a dated Oct-19 close series, not a live read). The decisive number - Q3 Cloud segment operating income versus nearly doubled depreciation - remains unfiled. Hold into the print.",
        "thesis": "Watch stance carried forward unchanged. Verified Q2-26 facts cut both ways: revenue +24% with operating income +30% (~34% margin), Cloud operating income $8.8B on $24.8B revenue and $513.9B Cloud backlog, versus H1 OCF-minus-capex compressed to ~$4.3B, Q2 capex ($44.9B) exceeding Q2 OCF ($39.1B), $49.6B common/preferred net proceeds, a $19.0B 6.25% mandatory convertible preferred, a $20.3B note issue and an authorized $40B ATM - all at a 5.1% 10Y and 5.43% 30Y compressing long-duration multiples. Q2 net income (+298%) is flattered by ~$99B unrealized equity gains and excluded. The tape gives no edge: RSI ~48, negative MACD histogram, price below the 20/50-day averages, ATR ~7.9 able to clear the band in one earnings session. The dispute - demand-driven accretive buildout versus equity-funded dilution before ROI proof - is settled by Q3 Cloud segment operating income versus depreciation and any capex guidance revision, neither yet available. Paying for either hypothesis pre-print remains uneconomic; holding cash is the resolution of an unresolved primary-evidenced dispute.",
        "countercase": "Bulls: the BofA note argues Cloud capacity growth and TPU sales could drive Q3 upside; the bar was reset low after the ~6% post-Q2 drop despite 82% reported Cloud growth; margin expansion outruns rate drag; the 200-day region held Monday at 338.25; debt and ~$1.2B/yr preferred dividends are trivial against ~$130B annualized operating income; backlog verifies contracted demand - so staged pre-print exposure captures a re-rating waiting forfeits. Bears: today's tech-led selloff on AI-investment fears and rising oil extends an inflation-shock backdrop that de-rates the complex; Meta's Oct-21 print is the read-across that could break the range before GOOG reports; the unmeasured Cloud outage hands skeptics pre-earnings ammunition; and near-zero H1 FCF with serial equity/hybrid funding makes the risk-reward symmetric, not skewed. Both cases remain credible and neither is confirmed by primary Q3 evidence.",
        "invalidation": "The hold resolves to action on specific events: (1) Q3-26 10-Q filing - verify Cloud segment operating income versus nearly doubled H1 depreciation ($9.5B to $13.6B), any capex guidance revision, and like-for-like backlog growth given the Q1-26 definition change; (2) earnings date confirmed via 8-K rather than social posts; (3) verified scope, duration and issuer statement on the Oct-20 Cloud outage; (4) Meta's Oct-21 results as the hyperscaler capex read-across; (5) price evidence - a decisive close below the 200-day (~338.9 on the dated Oct-19 series) on volume, or a range breakout above ~351 with Cloud-positive primary confirmation. Note the current quote at 337.60/337.68 sits marginally below that dated 200-day but is not a decisive volume-confirmed break, and the live packet's 60-session window lacks a 200-day calculation; treat the trigger as requiring the dated-series comparison plus volume confirmation. A close action still requires an owned position with a specifically invalidated thesis; none exists. Full-filing certification remains incomplete, which the owner has authorized for demo but which further justifies no directional exposure before primary Q3 numbers.",
